                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238214328",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198034691307",
                            "num_reviews": 40,
                            "playtime_forever": 773,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 773,
                            "last_played": 1792504116
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I enjoyed this game quite a bit! It's really effective as a puzzle game. They have almost zero handholding in terms of the game mechanics or even the goals, so for the first few rounds I didn't enjoy it particularly much and thought about giving up on it. However, after playing a bit more and figuring out the mechanics and goals a bit more, it became more addicting. Of course, I also like going for 100% achievements, so that kept me motivated, and I got better and better at the strategy and more sucked into the vague world-building, the longer I played. The puzzle mechanic really is unique and the minimalistic but well done graphics are fun and inviting. I'd definitely recommend this game to anyone who enjoys puzzle games a decent bit. Just don't give up within the first few rounds and I'm sure you'll also find a lot to enjoy!",
